  "id": "Compound::DB00540 - Gene::1565",
  "verbalization": "Nortriptyline is shown to interact with Cyp2e1 and Cyp2c9, both of which are involved in the metabolism of arachidonic acid. This interaction leads to the participation of these enzymes in the epoxygenation of arachidonic acid, a process that ultimately results in the participation of Cyp2d6. The evidence suggests a mechanistic pathway where Nortriptyline influences the activity of Cyp2e1 and Cyp2c9, which in turn modulate the activity of Cyp2d6 through shared enzymatic functions. The final scores from the paths indicate a consistent and plausible relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction between Nortriptyline and Cyp2d6 remains partially inferred. The observed evidence supports a role for Nortriptyline in modulating Cyp2d6 activity through a chain of enzymatic interactions involving arachidonic acid metabolism.",
